<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Book Library</title>
<style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}
body{margin:0;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#101827,#27405f);color:white}
header{text-align:center;padding:30px 20px;background:rgba(0,0,0,.3)}
header h1{margin:0 0 8px;font-size:34px}
header p{margin:0;color:#d7e5f5}
main{max-width:1050px;margin:auto;padding:30px 18px}
.library{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(260px,1fr));gap:20px}
.card,.reader{background:white;color:#172033;border-radius:16px;padding:24px;box-shadow:0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.25)}
.card h2,.reader h2{margin-top:0}
.author{color:#596579;margin-bottom:18px}
button{border:0;border-radius:10px;padding:11px 16px;background:#27405f;color:white;cursor:pointer;font-size:15px}
.reader{display:none;margin-top:0}
.back{margin-bottom:20px}
.story{white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px}
.note{margin-top:25px;padding:16px;border-left:4px solid #27405f;background:#eef3f8;color:#344054}
footer{text-align:center;padding:25px;color:#c8d4e2}
input:focus,textarea:focus{outline:2px solid #27405f}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
<h1>📚 Book Library</h1>
<p>A place for books submitted to the library.</p>
<div style="margin-top:18px;display:flex;gap:10px;justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap">
<button onclick="showSection('library')">📚 Browse Books</button>
<button onclick="showSection('submit')">✍️ Submit Your Book</button>
</div>
</header>
<main>
<section class="library" id="library">
<div class="card">
<h2>The Dusk Buster Adventures</h2>
<div class="author">By Sam Milne</div>
<button onclick="openBook()">Read Book</button>
</div>
</section>
<section class="reader" id="reader">
<button class="back" onclick="closeBook()">← Back to Books</button>
<h2>The Dusk Buster Adventures</h2>
<p><strong>By Sam Milne</strong></p>
<div class="story">Sam set out on his faithful ship, the Dusk Buster towards what he thought to be the tomb of Attila the Hun. Until this time, no one had been this close to finding the secret, triple coffin,  burial place of the ancient Mongolian’s tomb.  
 And after some years he saw ahead through the fog an island with a cave.
He looked anxiously at the tattered map he had been led by for years, could this be it?
After what seemed like an eternity He brought his long boat ashore.
He wrapped an oil soaked cloth around the end of a wooden club and lit it at the mouth of the cave. ,
He sees foot prints leading in after brushing off some cobwebs he went in two.
And he saw carvings of war tribes fighting with cities and walked in a little more, 
In to the cave and saw more carvings but instead of seeing more fighting he saw
Burial drawings and after entering a  corridor he saw oil lamps lit as if someone was expecting him. He put down his torch,  then turned to find the most confusing thing, he saw foot prints leading straight into a wall. It seemed as if the fog had cleared because the cave seemed a little brighter than before
And he noticed a little pond and in it was a coffin that seemed to be made of. . .gold?  
He became very excited and ran to get a rope [and the fog had cleared] and after a lot of doing [he had the help of his crew] it was out,  when it was open he found yet another coffin and he knew that this was the tomb of Attila, the Hun. And when he’d opened the third coffin he saw Attila the Hun.
After another lot of doing, they got the coffin out of the cave  
When they got home, Sam was still wondering why the outside coffin was made of gold,
He thought that the outer coffin was made of iron, then silver, then gold.
So, in two weeks he once again set out on his trusty long boat the dusk buster.
And when he got to the cave and stuck a few items in they turned  
To gold two, no one can know about this, said sam,I swear all of you to
Secrecy no one not even the king can know about this but one of them said,
But sir! Y-you can’t just do that! Why not?said Sam cooly,b-Because, it isn’t  right. master you can’t.
Then one of them shouted,hey!, What’s that! I think it’s a-a,well a Chinese  Dragon,
I think it is, what were we talking about? You were saying we can’t tell anybody about this.
 Your majesty, if I may have the pleasure of naming this island I would like to call it Death water island.  That’s a good name, said Sam.    
 And so they sailed home, and when Sam got home he had a hot bath and went  straight to bed.
 When he got up in the morning thinking about the foot prints and why they led to a wall.</div>
<div class="note">This is the first book in the library.</div>
</section>

<section id="submit" class="reader" style="display:none">
<button class="back" onclick="showSection('library')">← Back to Books</button>
<h2>✍️ Submit Your Book</h2>
<p>Have a story you want to share? Send in your own book for consideration.</p>

<form id="bookForm" onsubmit="prepareSubmission(event)">
<label><strong>Book Title</strong></label><br>
<input id="bookTitle" required style="width:100%;padding:12px;margin:7px 0 15px;border:1px solid #ccd3dc;border-radius:8px">

<label><strong>Author Name</strong></label><br>
<input id="bookAuthor" required style="width:100%;padding:12px;margin:7px 0 15px;border:1px solid #ccd3dc;border-radius:8px">

<label><strong>Short Description</strong></label><br>
<textarea id="bookDescription" rows="4" required style="width:100%;padding:12px;margin:7px 0 15px;border:1px solid #ccd3dc;border-radius:8px"></textarea>

<label><strong>Book / Story</strong></label><br>
<textarea id="bookStory" rows="14" required placeholder="Paste your book here..." style="width:100%;padding:12px;margin:7px 0 15px;border:1px solid #ccd3dc;border-radius:8px"></textarea>

<button type="submit">Prepare My Submission</button>
</form>

<div id="submissionResult" style="display:none;margin-top:20px;padding:16px;border-radius:10px;background:#eef3f8;color:#344054">
<strong>Your submission is ready.</strong>
<p id="submissionText"></p>
</div>

<div class="note">
Books are submitted for review first. A book should only be added to the public library after it has been reviewed and approved.
</div>
</section>
</main>
<footer>Book Library • More submitted books can be added later.</footer>
<script>
function openBook(){document.getElementById("library").style.display="none";document.getElementById("reader").style.display="block";window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function closeBook(){document.getElementById("reader").style.display="none";document.getElementById("library").style.display="grid";window.scrollTo(0,0)}
function showSection(section){
  document.getElementById("library").style.display = section === "library" ? "grid" : "none";
  document.getElementById("reader").style.display = "none";
  document.getElementById("submit").style.display = section === "submit" ? "block" : "none";
  window.scrollTo(0,0);
}
function prepareSubmission(event){
  event.preventDefault();
  const title=document.getElementById("bookTitle").value;
  const author=document.getElementById("bookAuthor").value;
  document.getElementById("submissionText").textContent =
    '"' + title + '" by ' + author + ' has been prepared for submission. The site owner can review it before adding it to the library.';
  document.getElementById("submissionResult").style.display="block";
}
</script>
</body>
</html>
